notes.body:
@pascal, @AndersBroman - do you have any thoughts about this?

For a given RAN-Function (e.g., KPM), there is backward-compatibility within the same major version - so 2.00, 2.01, 2.02 frames could all be dissected by 2.02 dissector.  To support multiple versions of KPM, I  create further versions as separate protocols under asn1, and have them register themselves as available to the main e2ap dissector.  When a session/conversation is setup, we find out which KPM OID/version is in the frame, so E2AP can select the best dissector to use for that conversion.  Unfortunately, there appears to be problems with the OIDs being the same over v1/v2/v3 for the RC RAN-Function.

However, one downside is that each of these separate RAN-Function dissectors needs to use some of the fields from E2SM, and this means we end up with a different filter for those fields from each RA-Function dissector.

